'' A literal too big for its type is fbc's warning 8, "Literal number too big, truncated".
'' Unsuffixed, a literal past 64 bits is tiko's int128 / uint128 (lexer/littype.tiko) and only
'' past 128 bits is too big (lines 1 and 6); with an integer suffix it is still past 64
'' (lines 2 and 4), the value fbc's. Lines 3 and 5 fit 128 bits and say nothing.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/literal-too-big.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/literal-too-big.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(1,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(2,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(4,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(6,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-NOT: (3,7): warning
'' EXPECT-NOT: (5,7): warning
